WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.380
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.880
What's wrong?  Scared?

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.810
I made a decision!

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.090
To take a new step forward with Flame!

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.970
A duelist like you must vanish from my sight.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.940
What?  The program is rewritten?

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.010
The area is disappearing.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.810
Running away?

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.390
C'mon!  Just when I was about to win.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.580
I reunited with Soulburner.  We'll log out.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:08.330
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:15.120
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:22.440
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.020
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:35.760
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:43.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:49.700
I want to share your pain

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.490
Yusaku!

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.720
You're going to see Kusanagi, right?

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.980
I'll go too!

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.890
I need to talk to him about-

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.700
Fujiki!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.940
Have a moment?  Huh?

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.140
It won't take much time.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.010
Sorry, but I'm busy.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:50.220
You sure you want to say that?

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.350
It's important.  I want 
to talk about your secret.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.250
Don't worry about me.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:01.080
I'll go ahead.  See you later!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.060
What do you want to talk about?

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.330
Not here.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.500
Let's go somewhere else.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:18.440
What a nice day.  As usual.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.440
Yusaku is at school and 
Kusanagi's shop is empty.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.580
It's so peaceful!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.330
Hey!  Come down!

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.320
I'll give you something nice!

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.240
Something nice?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.780
I'm counting on you!

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.500
Do ten laps around the city!

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.740
Ten?  Are you punishing me?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.510
I'll charge you for this gig!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.810
Huh?  That's Takeru.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.240
He's going to see Kusanagi?

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.010
Why isn't Yusaku with him?

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.160
Takeru is alone...

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.490
Flame must've gotten important info-

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:13.720
Ouch...  What just happened?

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.070
Why did a Duel Disk fall from the sky?

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.280
Den City is incredible.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.080
You can just pick up Duel Disks!

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.660
Wrong!  I fell!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.650
What?

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.920
Ai, you can fly?

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.620
Ai fly!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.160
Is that a pun?

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.080
Takeru, I thought of something nice!

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.890
Put wheels on this Disk!

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.440
And an engine.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.700
Then you won't need train fare 
to go home to the countryside.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.370
No.  Seriously, stop.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.610
Hey, Takeru.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.980
You came.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.180
Kusanagi!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.480
Thank you for last time.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.810
Thanks to you, I was able to log out.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.890
I brought you a gift.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:15.290
It's not worth thanking me over.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.930
That's a hamburger!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.200
You shouldn't bring that to a hot dog stand.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.670
Quiet!

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:28.340
It's important to taste test your rivals.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.670
Thank you.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.800
I'll take it.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.160
I'll get you coffee.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.500
Umm...

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.050
An unrelated question, but where's Yusaku?

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:45.300
He's with some classmate named Shima.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.860
To talk about something important.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.820
Shima?  I have a bad feeling about this.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.510
Hey, Fujiki.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:06:00.120
I'm Playmaker's soulmate, right?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.400
Really?

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.580
C'mon, you know that.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.720
I know your secret!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:18.740
If you don't want me to reveal your 
secret, you should listen to my request.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.120
Thanks for the meal.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.130
This place is always impressive to see.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.300
All your equipment's in here?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.050
Equipment doesn't matter for hacking.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.940
What's important is... in here.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:40.910
But I'm no match for Yusaku.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:44.900
You two are the perfect team for LINK VRAINS.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.060
A duelist and a hacker who provides backup.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.250
Speaking of...

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:53.880
Why did Kusanagi and 
Yusaku decide to team up?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.980
I never heard the story.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:00.230
That's a story I'm interested in.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.020
Kusanagi, will you tell us?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.250
Well, there's a lot to the story.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.470
C'mon!

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:14.450
Tell us the story of how 
Yusaku and Kusanagi met!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:18.240
C'mon, Kusanagi!

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.950
Well...

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:26.420
Since you're helping me with my brother, 
I guess it's fine if you know about us.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.780
But to do that...

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.630
I have to start with that incident.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.010
You mean the Lost Incident?

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:42.810
Yeah.  Takeru, my story may 
remind you about your past.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.740
I don't mind.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:51.520
As someone who also suffered from that 
incident, please let me hear the story.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.730
Okay.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.960
During the six months that Jin was missing...

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:03.280
...my parents and I were sad, but 
we also feverishly searched for Jin.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:10.380
When I heard that they found my brother, 
I thought all my hardships were over.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:15.400
But it was only the beginning 
of more hardship.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.880
Jin!  Welcome home!

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:20.410
I was worried about you.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.880
Where were you?

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.350
Hey Jin!  Why so quiet?

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.820
Did you fall asleep?

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:36.760
Jin used to be gentle and cheerful.

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.580
But he totally changed.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.870
I wanted to learn what 
happened to my brother.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:50.680
But as you know, they 
didn't capture Dr. Kogami.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:55.120
And the incident was covered up.

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:00.580
But that incited me into becoming a hacker.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.730
To know the whole story 
about the Lost Incident,

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.790
I had to hone my hacking skills 
to uncover the secret info.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.310
I used to focus on sports,

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:19.240
but I gave that up to study 
programming and network techniques.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:26.330
I polished my skills until I 
could hack into most servers.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:32.800
I discovered that the Knights of 
Hanoi were behind the incident.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.260
And that they show up in LINK VRAINS.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:43.390
So I created my own avatar 
and went to LINK VRAINS.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:50.700
And I learned that the Knights of Hanoi were 
collecting cards known as Cyberse-Type.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.180
It's over!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.440
Who are you?

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:03.760
Our goal is to destroy Cyberse cards!

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.190
Since you've seen us, we must now erase you.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.020
What are you going to do?

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.980
You already know.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:17.660
We'll erase your account and prevent you 
from logging into LINK VRAINS again.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.300
What?

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.500
You're kidding, right?

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.870
Delete.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.940
Mission complete.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.240
Let's head to the next target.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.350
You there!  Come on out!

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.850
We know you're hiding there!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.620
Stop!

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.300
Don't let him escape!  After him!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.760
He turned that corner!

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.280
It's a dead end!  He's trapped!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.000
Hey you!

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.550
This way!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.120
Hurry!  Do you want them to catch you?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.260
Hurry!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.370
Right.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.240
He's not here!

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.860
Damn!  He escaped!

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.560
But how?

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.270
Maybe he's over there.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:39.970
That was close.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.250
Thank you.  You saved me.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.280
I'm Unnamed.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:47.720
What's your name?

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.190
I'm Unknown.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:53.930
We're similar.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:54.900
You...

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.030
Don't you know the Knights 
of Hanoi are dangerous?

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.460
I know they're dangerous!

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:04.660
But I need to know.

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:10.990
I need info to help my dear brother!

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.240
Brother?

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:18.740
Yeah.  My brother was involved in 
an incident that damaged his soul.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:22.850
The Knights of Hanoi 
aren't ordinary duelists.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.180
Leave this place immediately.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.120
Wait, Unknown!

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.990
Have you heard about the Lost Incident?

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:34.470
Who knows.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:38.870
If you value your life, log out immediately.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.260
That was my first meeting with Yusaku.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.920
I still went to LINK VRAINS to gather info.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:59.920
You didn't heed Yusaku's 
warning?  Nice, Kusanagi!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.900
You cared more about learning 
the truth than your own safety.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:11.420
Exactly.  But at my level of dueling skills, 
facing the Knights of Hanoi was too dangerous.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.110
Found him!

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:15.640
He won't escape this time!

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.890
It's over for me.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.320
Jin...

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.280
Run!

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:40.230
Jin?

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.240
Unknown!

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.240
Unknown!

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:52.210
Why did you come back?

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.330
I know you're worried about your brother.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.760
But don't bear the burden alone.

00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:02.150
What happened to your 
brother isn't your fault.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.570
But!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:09.390
If something happens to you here, 
who will protect your brother?

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.570
Leave this to me.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.300
Okay.  Thanks.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:18.050
But you can't log out right now.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:22.640
The Knights of Hanoi create an area 
that stops you from logging out.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:26.500
But the affected area isn't that big.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.350
If you can get there, you can log out.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:31.890
Go!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.290
Leave this to me!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.120
Log out!

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.430
Unknown!

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:53.280
I heard there was someone 
interfering with our affairs.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.440
Seems that person is you.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:15:00.440
Since you're here, we'll erase you.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.850
Guys, I'll handle him.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:06.250
Bring it on!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.220
Duel!

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.410
What happened to him?

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.200
Is he okay?

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.680
There he is!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.330
I'll go first!  My turn!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.840
You're a fool to oppose the Knights of Hanoi!

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:29.810
I'll quickly turn you into LINK VRAINS dust!

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:34.210
I summon Jack Wyvern from my hand!

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.800
I equip the Equip Spell, Big 
Bang Shot on Jack Wyvern.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:45.040
The equipped monster gains 400 ATK.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:50.730
Then I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.190
It's your turn.  Bring it on.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:59.300
Even though there's no way you can defeat me.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:03.310
I don't intend to lose against anyone!

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.680
Not until I fulfill my revenge!

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:09.360
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:15.130
When there are no monsters on my field, 
I can Special Summon this card.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.020
Appear, Photon Thrasher!

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.230
Then I summon Marauding Captain!

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:35.040
When it's summoned, I can Special Summon 
a Level 4 or lower monster from my hand.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:37.800
Appear, Exarion Universe!

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:45.080
No matter how many low ATK 
weaklings you line up...

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:49.090
...you can't fight my 
monster on equal footing.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.690
Are you sure?

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:52.670
What?

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.960
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:58.680
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.880
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters!

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:09.020
I set Photon Thrasher, Marauding Captain 
and Exarion Universe in the Link Markers!

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.760
Circuit combine!

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.620
Link Summon!

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:19.480
Appear, Link 3 Gaia Saber, 
the Lightning Shadow!

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.490
Link Summon?

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:24.520
Battle!

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:28.740
Gaia Saber, the Lightning 
Shadow attacks Jack Wyvern!

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.410
It's no use!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:34.160
I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, Limiter Removal!

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:39.640
It doubles the ATK of all Machines on 
my field until the end of the turn!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:46.370
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, 
Forbidden Lance from my hand!

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:53.490
One faceup monster loses 800 
ATK until the end of the turn.

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:58.160
And that monster can't be affected 
by any other spells or traps!

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:58.860
What?

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:06.800
Big Bang Shot so Limiter Removal's effects 
vanish, and Jack Wyvern loses 1200 ATK!

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.880
Then I activate Limiter Removal from my hand!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:15.710
It doubles Gaia Saber's ATK!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:19.440
5200 ATK?

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:23.980
Go, Gaia Saber!  Spiral Spear!

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:35.990
You have no right to call yourself a duelist!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:40.100
He has something that I lack.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.610
Overwhelming power for this world.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:47.910
He's definitely someone I need!

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:51.950
Why do you oppose us?

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:55.970
Do you know about the Lost Incident?

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:57.500
Lost Incident?

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:59.100
What are you talking about?

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:05.540
We're only hunting Cyberse to demonstrate 
Hanoi's power in the network world.

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:09.290
It's a waste of time to ask you.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.520
I can't waste time playing with you.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:15.300
After him!  Don't let him escape!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:22.270
Unknown is also investigating 
the Lost Incident.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:30.680
Unknown!

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:33.680
You're trapped!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.890
Give up.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:42.360
Unknown!  Up!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.550
Jump!

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.820
Unknown, when you return to the real world...

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:56.300
...make sure to visit Café Nagi.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.510
Café Nagi?

00:19:57.510 --> 00:20:00.460
Yeah.  It's in Den City.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:03.520
Thanks as always.

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.280
Thanks.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.850
Please come again.

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.890
Welcome.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.360
One hot dog.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.450
Okay.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.510
Here you go.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:26.970
Wait up!

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.280
Hurry!

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:32.220
Umm...

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.770
You saved me.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:37.960
Thank you, Unnamed.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.420
Unnamed...  Wait!

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:49.770
I didn't expect Unknown to be so young.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.830
Were you involved in the Lost Incident?

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.430
My brother is a victim.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:03.170
The incident hurt him emotionally, 
and he still wanders in darkness.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:08.560
I want to know what happened to him!

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:15.120
If I do, I may be able to 
understand his suffering.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:23.870
When you saved me, I could envision 
my brother growing strong like you.

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:30.030
Please help me save my brother!

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:34.770
I'm Shoichi Kusanagi!  
Please team up with me!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:39.800
If you're the strongest spear 
to fight the Knights of Hanoi...

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:43.510
...I'll be the strongest 
shield to protect you!

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:46.520
Please, Unknown!

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:52.780
Okay.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.430
Let's work together.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.930
My name is Fujiki.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:02.340
Yusaku Fujiki.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:25.940
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:32.640
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:36.140
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:39.280
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:43.880
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:46.850
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.560 --> 00:22:57.730
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.870
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:04.810
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:04.970 --> 00:23:10.760
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:14.050
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.840
There's a dungeon containing a Cyberse Deck.

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:46.700
We lacked any leads back then, so we 
had to rely on untrustworthy rumors.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:54.080
No matter how difficult the path, we 
believed we'd reach the truth if we kept fighting.

00:23:54.080 --> 00:23:58.020
This may be our secret weapon 
to use against the Hanoi!

00:23:58.020 --> 00:24:02.280
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Playmaker's Breath

00:24:02.280 --> 00:24:04.460
Into the VRAINS!
